{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetPsnspf5Hnde5NRzm4D","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have sufficient understanding of the codebase. Let me complete the ANALYSIS phase:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n\n- `Order.kt:11-16` — Order data class has no status field; needs to add ACTIVE and CANCELLED states\n- `OrderController.kt:17-46` — Has create (POST), getById (GET), and list (GET); needs cancel endpoint\n- `OrderRepository.kt:11-27` — In-memory store with standard CRUD operations\n- `Shipment.kt:9-14` — Already has status field with enum ShipmentStatus (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- `ShipmentController.kt:22-56` — Has create (POST), getById (GET), and list (GET)\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt:11-27` — In-memory store; needs method to find shipments by orderId\n- `api/ApiExceptions.kt:18-24` — ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409) exist\n- `api/ApiError.kt:31-37` — ErrorCode enum has ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED\n- `api/GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:16-28` — Centralized exception-to-response mapping\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n\n- All domain logic uses exceptions from `api/ApiExceptions.kt` (ResourceNotFoundException for 404, ConflictException for 409)\n- All error responses follow the ApiError envelope: `{ error: { code, message, fields } }`\n- Controllers throw exceptions directly; GlobalExceptionHandler converts them to responses\n- Tests verify both HTTP status **and** error envelope code via jsonPath\n- Tests exercise both positive and negative cases\n- Tests use MockMvc with separate assertions on status and body\n- In-memory repositories using ConcurrentHashMap\n\n**Affected files:**\n\n1. `Order.kt` — Add status field and enum OrderStatus (ACTIVE, CANCELLED); required because the ticket names order status\n2. `OrderController.kt` — Add `POST /{orderId}/cancel` endpoint; required because the ticket names this endpoint\n3. `ShipmentRepository.kt` — Add `findByOrderId(orderId)` method; required to find shipments to cancel\n4. `ShipmentController.kt` — Add validation to reject shipment creation for CANCELLED orders; required by ticket requirement\n5. `api/ApiError.kt` — Add error codes for ORDER_CANCELLED and ORDER_CANCEL_BLOCKED; required for new error scenarios\n6. `OrderControllerTest.kt` — Add tests for cancel endpoint and status reporting; required for acceptance criteria\n7. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Add test for shipment creation rejection on cancelled order; required by ticket\n\n**Risks:**\n\n- Cancel operation must be all-or-nothing: if any shipment is CONFIRMED, nothing changes (order stays ACTIVE, all shipments keep their status)\n- Idempotent retry: cancelling an already-cancelled order must succeed and return the order, not fail\n- Order not found case must return 404 before any changes\n- Race conditions between checking shipment status and cancelling them (mitigated by single-threaded test execution, but in production this would need transaction support)\n\n**Open questions:**\n\n1. Should the error code for \"cannot cancel order with confirmed shipments\" be `ORDER_CANCEL_BLOCKED` or reuse an existing code? → I'll use `ORDER_CANCEL_BLOCKED` as it clearly names the reason\n2. Should the error code for \"cannot create shipment for cancelled order\" be `ORDER_CANCELLED` or something else? → I'll use `ORDER_CANCELLED` as it's concise\n\nNow I'll move to DESIGN.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Add `status: OrderStatus` field to Order data class; add OrderStatus enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED values. New orders default to ACTIVE.\n\n2. **api/ApiError.kt** — Add two error codes to ErrorCode enum:\n   - `ORDER_CANCEL_BLOCKED` — when cancel is rejected because a shipment is CONFIRMED\n   - `ORDER_CANCELLED` — when shipment creation is rejected because the order is CANCELLED\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to query shipments by order.\n\n4. **OrderController.kt** — Add `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` endpoint that:\n   - Takes orderId as path variable\n   - Returns the cancelled order as response body\n   - Throws ResourceNotFoundException if order doesn't exist\n   - Throws ConflictException with ORDER_CANCEL_BLOCKED if any shipment is CONFIRMED\n   - Changes order status to CANCELLED and cancels all CREATED shipments\n   - Succeeds idempotently if order is already CANCELLED (changes nothing, returns the order)\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** — Modify the create endpoint to:\n   - Check if the target order exists and is not CANCELLED\n   - Throw ConflictException with ORDER_CANCELLED if order is CANCELLED\n   - (Keep existing check for duplicate shipment ID)\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Add tests covering:\n   - Cancel an ACTIVE order → transitions to CANCELLED, returns cancelled order, GET shows CANCELLED status\n   - Cancel an ACTIVE order with CREATED shipments → cancels all CREATED shipments, GET shows CANCELLED status and shipment shows CANCELLED\n   - Cancel an ACTIVE order with a CONFIRMED shipment → rejects with 409 ORDER_CANCEL_BLOCKED, order stays ACTIVE, shipments unchanged (verified by GET)\n   - Cancel an already CANCELLED order → succeeds, changes nothing, returns order with CANCELLED status\n   - Cancel a non-existent order → rejects with 404 ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add test:\n   - Create shipment for a CANCELLED order → rejects with 409 ORDER_CANCELLED\n\n**Alternative I rejected:**\n\nI considered adding an OrderService class to encapsulate the cancel logic and shipment queries, but the existing codebase has no service layer (logic is in controllers). Adding one would violate the convention of \"preserve existing architecture\" and add unrelated refactoring. The cancel logic is straightforward enough to fit in the controller.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Cancel ACTIVE order, no CONFIRMED shipments:**\n   - Request: `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel`\n   - Controller retrieves order from repo, finds all shipments by orderId, checks none are CONFIRMED\n   - Updates order status to CANCELLED, updates all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED\n   - Returns: 200 OK with order body showing status=CANCELLED\n   - Stored: Order and shipments persist with new status\n\n2. **Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment:**\n   - Request: `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel`\n   - Controller retrieves order, finds shipments, sees CONFIRMED status\n   - Throws ConflictException with code ORDER_CANCEL_BLOCKED, message naming the blocked state\n   - Returns: 409 CONFLICT with error envelope\n   - Stored: Nothing changes (all-or-nothing)\n\n3. **Cancel already CANCELLED order:**\n   - Request: `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel`\n   - Controller retrieves order, sees status is CANCELLED\n   - No changes needed\n   - Returns: 200 OK with order body showing status=CANCELLED\n   - Stored: Nothing changes (idempotent)\n\n4. **Cancel non-existent order:**\n   - Request: `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel`\n   - Controller tries to find order, gets null\n   - Throws ResourceNotFoundException with code ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n   - Returns: 404 NOT FOUND with error envelope\n   - Stored: Nothing changes\n\n5. **Create shipment for CANCELLED order:**\n   - Request: `POST /shipments` with orderId of CANCELLED order\n   - Controller finds order, sees status is CANCELLED\n   - Throws ConflictException with code ORDER_CANCELLED\n   - Returns: 409 CONFLICT with error envelope\n   - Stored: Nothing changes\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n- **OrderControllerTest: cancel active order** — exercises cancel path, asserts response body has order with CANCELLED status, GETs the order and verifies persisted status\n- **OrderControllerTest: cancel with created shipments** — creates CREATED shipments, cancels order, GETs shipments and verifies they're CANCELLED\n- **OrderControllerTest: cancel blocked by confirmed shipment** — creates a CONFIRMED shipment (written directly to repo), cancels order, asserts 409 with ORDER_CANCEL_BLOCKED code, GETs order and verifies it's still ACTIVE, GETs shipment and verifies it's still CONFIRMED\n- **OrderControllerTest: cancel already cancelled** — cancels order, cancels again, asserts 200 response (idempotent), verifies no change via GET\n- **OrderControllerTest: cancel nonexistent** — cancels unknown order, asserts 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND code\n- **OrderControllerTest: new order is active** — creates order, GETs it, asserts status is ACTIVE (ensures default works)\n- **ShipmentControllerTest: create shipment for cancelled order** — cancels an order, tries to create shipment for it, asserts 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED code, GETs order and verifies no shipment was created\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nI'll now make the minimal set of changes needed to satisfy the design:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1232,"cache_read_input_tokens":22656,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1232},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0afe650d-da04-4fce-bd6a-ebfd7f54610d","uuid":"49849963-0072-4e23-9101-ac99a3f1896a","timestamp":"2026-09-09T19:11:39.928Z","request_id":"req_011CetPsnG7VyXV9atNhEZum"}
