{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetQ2SeejZeScJWhGFTBr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! All tests pass. Command run: `./mvnw test` from `sample-service/` directory. Result: **BUILD SUCCESS** with 20 tests passing, 0 failures, 0 errors.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n```\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✅ **Existing build passes** — `./mvnw test` completed with BUILD SUCCESS\n2. ✅ **Existing tests pass** — All original tests in OrderControllerTest (4), ShipmentControllerTest (5), CustomerControllerTest (3), and SampleServiceApplicationTests (1) still pass\n3. ✅ **`POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` cancels an active order, persists it, and cancels `CREATED` shipments** — Test \"cancels an active order and returns the cancelled order\" verifies persistence via GET; test \"cancels all created shipments when cancelling an order\" verifies shipment cancellation and persistence\n4. ✅ **Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API** — Uses ConflictException (409) and ResourceNotFoundException (404) with ErrorCode enum following existing patterns; GlobalExceptionHandler formats all responses identically\n5. ✅ **Repeated cancel succeeds; cancel blocked by CONFIRMED shipment changes nothing; unknown order is refused; shipment for cancelled order is refused** — Tests verify: \"idempotently succeeds when cancelling an already-cancelled order\" (idempotent); \"rejects cancel if a shipment is confirmed and leaves everything unchanged\" (all-or-nothing verified by separate GETs); \"rejects cancel of nonexistent order with 404\"; \"rejects shipment creation for a cancelled order\"\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency appears** — pom.xml unchanged\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** — Only modified: Order.kt, OrderController.kt, OrderRepository.kt (via ShipmentRepository addition), ShipmentController.kt, ShipmentRepository.kt, ApiError.kt, plus corresponding test files\n\n**Diff review — every changed file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Added `status: OrderStatus` field (required), OrderStatus enum with ACTIVE/CANCELLED (required). Change was necessary and minimal.\n\n2. **ApiError.kt** — Added ORDER_CANCEL_BLOCKED and ORDER_CANCELLED error codes (required for new error scenarios named by the ticket). Change was necessary.\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Added `findByOrderId()` query method (required to find shipments during cancel operation). Change was necessary.\n\n4. **OrderController.kt** — Added `cancel()` endpoint and injected ShipmentRepository (required). Endpoint implements all requirements: rejects nonexistent orders (404), rejects if CONFIRMED shipment exists (409), cancels CREATED shipments, handles idempotent repeat. Change was necessary.\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** — Added check to reject shipment creation for CANCELLED orders, injected OrderRepository (required). Change was necessary.\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Added 6 new tests covering: status field defaults to ACTIVE, cancel success with persistence verification via separate GET, cancel with shipment cancellation verified via separate GETs, cancel blocked by CONFIRMED shipment with all-or-nothing verification via separate GETs, idempotent retry, and nonexistent order rejection with error code check. All follow the testing-and-verification skill patterns (response body assertions, separate GET after mutation, separate GET after refusal, error code assertions).\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Added 1 new test covering shipment creation rejection for cancelled order with verification that shipment was not created via separate GET request, plus error code assertion. Follows testing-and-verification patterns.\n\n**Unresolved findings:**\n\nNone. All acceptance criteria are satisfied, all tests pass, and no files outside the required set were modified.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement: Add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that transitions